#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Python.rst:15
msgid "Writing Basic Tests with Python - tutorial"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Python.rst:18
msgid ""
"Basic Python tests help verify package behavior while developing and "
"maintaining ROS code. This article shows how to add pytest tests to an "
"``ament_python`` package. After you follow these steps, you can organize "
"test files, add test dependencies, and run selected tests with ``colcon``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Python.rst:26
msgid ""
"Starting point: we'll assume you have a :ref:`basic ament_python "
"package<CreatePkg>` set up already and you want to add some tests to it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Python.rst:28
msgid ""
"If you are using ament_cmake_python, refer to the :doc:`ament_cmake_python "
"docs <../../Build/Ament-CMake-Python-Documentation>` for how to make tests "
"discoverable. The test contents and invocation with ``colcon`` remain the "
"same."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Python.rst:32
msgid "Package Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Python.rst:35
msgid "setup.py"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Python.rst:37
msgid ""
"Your ``setup.py`` must have a test dependency on ``pytest`` within the call "
"to ``setup(...)``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Python.rst:39
msgid ""
"extras_require={\n"
"    'test': ['pytest'],\n"
"},"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Python.rst:46
msgid "Test Files and Folders"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Python.rst:48
msgid ""
"Your test code needs to go in a folder named ``tests`` in the root of your "
"package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Python.rst:50
msgid ""
"Any file that contains tests that you want to run must have the pattern "
"``test_FOO.py`` where ``FOO`` can be replaced with anything."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Python.rst:53
msgid "Example package layout:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Python.rst:55
msgid ""
"awesome_ros_package/\n"
"  awesome_ros_package/\n"
"      __init__.py\n"
"      fozzie.py\n"
"  package.xml\n"
"  setup.cfg\n"
"  setup.py\n"
"  tests/\n"
"      test_init.py\n"
"      test_copyright.py\n"
"      test_fozzie.py"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Python.rst:71
msgid "Test Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Python.rst:73
msgid ""
"You can now write tests to your heart's content. There are `plenty of "
"resources on pytest <https://docs.pytest.org>`__, but in short, you can "
"write functions with the ``test_`` prefix and include whatever assert "
"statements you'd like."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Python.rst:77
msgid ""
"def test_math():\n"
"    assert 2 + 2 == 5   # This should fail for most mathematical systems"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Python.rst:83
msgid "Running Tests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Python.rst:85
msgid ""
"See the :doc:`tutorial on how to run tests from the command line <CLI>` for "
"more information on running the tests and inspecting the test results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Python.rst:88
msgid "Special Commands"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Python.rst:90
msgid ""
"Beyond the :doc:`standard colcon testing commands <CLI>` you can also "
"specify arguments to the ``pytest`` framework from the command line with the "
"``--pytest-args`` flag. For example, you can specify the name of the "
"function to run with"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Python.rst:96
msgid "Linux/macOS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Python.rst:98
msgid ""
"$ colcon test --packages-select <name-of-pkg> --pytest-args -k "
"name_of_the_test_function"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Python.rst:102
msgid "Windows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Python.rst:104
msgid ""
"$ colcon test --merge-install --packages-select <name-of-pkg> --pytest-args -"
"k name_of_the_test_function"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Python.rst:108
msgid "To see the pytest output while running the tests, use these flags:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Python.rst:110
msgid "$ colcon test --event-handlers console_cohesion+"
msgstr ""
